{"Using Error level for informational messages will pollute error logs and potentially trigger false alerts in production monitoring. These cleanup progress messages should use Debug level since they're routine operations.": 0.9552852511405945, "Ticker interval reduced from 10 minutes to 1 minute, but the cleanup timeout is still 9 minutes. This 10x increase in cleanup frequency is unrelated to the stated PR goal and could significantly increase database load. Either the timeout constant should also be updated, or this is a debugging change that was accidentally included.": 0.9569093585014343, "Register t.Cleanup immediately after createTestAnnotations, before the setup-verification assertions. If assertAnnotationCount or assertAnnotationTagCount fails, the cleanup callback is never registered, leaving stale rows in the shared database and causing cascading failures in subsequent subtests.": 0.9240627288818359}